## Build 3b closes the uncommittable Build 3 lensed-likelihood fast path by fixing the ACCURACY DEFECT first, then landing one hook-clean commit. Root cause of the defect (Professor): _coarse_w_node_grid in cogwheel/lensing/likelihood.py places kernel-interpolation transition nodes only at REAL-image delay separations, but each channel kernel K_a(w) has its smootherstep structure at RHO_END/delta_full where delta_full is the FULL-CLUSTER separation (real + virtual/parked labels) — the exact real-vs-full-cluster pattern already fixed in _channel_switch (F008). Because the grid misplaces nodes, the two-image config converges only by brute node count (pure log-spacing needs ~100+ nodes to reach null-safe 1e-3), so the shipped _DEFAULT_KERNEL_NODES=10 leaks up to 3.44 nats on the kappa config (gate RB_ATOL=1.5). WP1 accelerates geometry.nearest_caustic_point (a ~29 ms/eval frequency-INDEPENDENT scipy caustic search that recomputes the astroid-caustic distance every evaluate) by njit-ing a lightweight source-only caustic evaluator and vectorizing the coarse scan (value-preserving: distance rel<1e-10 / <=2 ULP, identical branch selection); this also makes cheap virtual-label delays available. WP2 (depends on WP1) extends _coarse_w_node_grid to place transition nodes at full-cluster separations, sets _DEFAULT_KERNEL_NODES=40, and deletes the false 'clears interpolation gate (F within 1e-8)' comment. The contraction-speedup lever from the brief is DELIBERATELY DROPPED: per Professor+Simplifier the ~2.3 ms/point F_op cost is a real FLOP floor (order-40 explicit 85x85 njit contraction), the only bit-safe lever (skip exact-zero table coeffs) yields ~20-30% for real F005 risk, and few-ms is UNREACHABLE this build without the deferred 2D surrogate table. HONEST TIMING OUTCOME: with the correct ~40-node grid, single-thread warm lnlike is ~110 ms (SLOWER than Build 3's 70 ms, but CORRECT) — this measured floor is to be documented in the change report and the 2D-table decision escalated to the owner; NO tolerance widening, NO silently-moved ceiling. Test re-aiming (Test Developer, domain_test_descriptions) moves the RB-vs-brute and interpolation gates onto the PRODUCTION node grid with a null-safe metric, inverts SelfFalsification, and pins timing to single thread. DOC-SYNC (NOT a Coder WP, per architect rules): SPEC.md must gain the new test module test_lensing_fast_path.py and note the node-grid accuracy fix; changelog/completed/spec_changelog fragments, scripts/render_fragments.py, and completion of todo.d/engine_hyp1f1-surrogate.md are handled by the post-gate doc-sync/Librarian phase so the spec/doc pre-commit hook passes without --no-verify. ASSUMPTIONS: (1) base=40 + full-cluster placement clears null-safe<1e-3 and RB<=1.5 on every config (Professor's physics + the n=82-log-spaced->1.1e-3 convergence data plus the placement improvement; if the gate shows 40 short, the proven-safe fallback is to raise the base toward ~82 — surfaced by the gate, not by Coder measurement); (2) production network SNR ~20 for the |delta_lnL| ~ rho^2 * null-safe mapping.

### WP1: Accelerate the frequency-independent caustic search (geometry.nearest_caustic_point)
  What: Eliminate the ~29 ms/eval, frequency-independent cost of geometry.nearest_caustic_point (256-point scipy coarse scan + 4 bounded minimize_scalar refinements, each making ~330 Python-level critical_point calls that each do an np.linalg.eigh and frame construction) WITHOUT changing its returned values or the downstream wave/geometric branch decisions. This is the prerequisite that makes cheap virtual-label delays available to WP2.
  Where: cogwheel/lensing/chang_refsdal/geometry.py — nearest_caustic_point (and a new module-private njit helper). Read-only reference: critical_point, macro_matrix, hessian, delay, and channels.py select_branch / _min_delay_separation / _channel_switch to confirm branch invariance.
  How: Add a numba.njit(cache=True, fastmath=False) helper `_caustic_source(theta, gamma, beta, kappa)` that reproduces EXACTLY the arithmetic of critical_point that produces its `.source` attribute ONLY — i.e. lam=1-kappa, effective_gamma=gamma/lam, phase=theta-beta, effective_u = effective_gamma*cos(2*phase)+sqrt(1-effective_gamma^2*sin(2*phase)^2), radius=1/sqrt(lam*effective_u), image=radius*[cos(theta),sin(theta)], source = macro_matrix@image - image/radius^2 — SKIPPING the np.linalg.eigh, eigenframe, and det-orientation work that critical_point does (the distance search needs only the caustic source point). Keep the LensDomainError positive-parity guard (1-kappa>|gamma|) at the top of nearest_caustic_point (raised before any njit call). Vectorize the coarse scan: compute squared distances at all n_grid polar angles either with a njit loop or a vectorized numpy expression built on the same per-theta arithmetic, so the argsort->top-4 cell selection is bit-identical to today. KEEP scipy.optimize.minimize_scalar bounded (xatol=1e-12) for the 4 refinements (Simplifier: a hand-rolled njit minimizer is over-engineering — the bottleneck was the Python-boundary critical_point calls, not the minimizer arithmetic), but pass it a Python closure over the njit `_caustic_source` so each objective eval is cheap. After finding the best theta, make ONE full critical_point(gamma, theta, beta, kappa) call to build the returned NearestCausticPoint (image, source, hard_axis, soft_axis, hard_value, distance) so the frame/eigenvalue are byte-identical to today. Value-preservation acceptance (Professor authority, relaxing the brief's literal 2-ULP to the physically-necessary bound): the returned distance agrees to relative < 1e-10 (target <=2 ULP; cos/sin/sqrt may differ by ~1 ULP between numba libm and numpy) AND the wave-vs-geometric branch selected by channels.select_branch is IDENTICAL for every input in the existing engine + fast-path suites. Multiple-minimum case (source on an astroid symmetry axis) is benign: the 4 near-equal minima are related by the astroid's discrete symmetry, so any global minimum returns the same distance and the same virtual-label delay. Do NOT alter n_grid (256) or the 4-cell refinement count.
  Who: Coder
  Verification: geometry.py exposes a njit source-only `_caustic_source` helper; nearest_caustic_point keeps the 256-point coarse scan + 4 bounded scipy refinements and builds its returned frame/eigenvalue from a single final critical_point call; the returned caustic distance agrees to relative < 1e-10 with an independent dense brute-force minimization and the wave/geometric branch selection is unchanged across the engine + fast-path suites; the per-eval caustic cost drops from ~29 ms to < 1 ms; the LensDomainError positive-parity guard and all F005/refusal behaviour are byte-identical.
  Max turns: 60

### WP2: Fix the kernel node grid for correctness (full-cluster transition placement + default)
  What: Repair the under-resolution accuracy defect so production RB-vs-brute lnlike stays <= 1.5 nat on every _LENS_CONFIGS row with the SHIPPED default node grid, by placing interpolation transition nodes at the frequencies where the channel kernels actually have structure (full-cluster separations), and by setting an honest default node count. Delete the false accuracy comment.
  Where: cogwheel/lensing/likelihood.py — _coarse_w_node_grid, the _DEFAULT_KERNEL_NODES constant + its docstring comment, and _amplification_coefficients wiring. Read-only reference: channels._channel_switch and _min_delay_separation (the F008 full-cluster rule to mirror), channels.real_image_delays, geometry.nearest_caustic_point / geometry.delay.
  How: 1) Extend _coarse_w_node_grid so the mandatory transition nodes RHO_START/delta and RHO_END/delta are placed at FULL-CLUSTER pairwise delay separations, not real-image-only separations. The full cluster = real-image delays (already from real_image_delays) UNION the virtual/parked-label delays at the nearest critical point — mirror channels._channel_switch's F008 full-cluster neighbour set exactly (min over ALL cluster labels except self, including virtual labels). Obtain the virtual-label delays cheaply from the geometry: call geometry.nearest_caustic_point (now cheap after WP1) and take the Fermat delay at its critical point via geometry.delay(critical_point.image, source, matrix); do NOT run an engine sweep to get them. Keep the existing union-with-log-spaced-base + np.unique(sorted, strictly-increasing, all > w_min > 0) structure and the branch-switch node RHO_END/delta_min (now over full-cluster delta_min). This is a PLACEMENT correction, NOT a new config-adaptive-count abstraction (Simplifier: adaptive count trimmed). 2) Set _DEFAULT_KERNEL_NODES = 40 (base log-spaced count). Provenance (Professor + measured convergence table): pure log-spacing needs ~100+ nodes to clear null-safe 1e-3 on the two-image config (n=82 gives 1.1e-3), because it misses the full-cluster kernel structure; the full-cluster placement adds nodes exactly at RHO_END/delta_full where two-image's binding structure lives, so base=40 + placement clears null-safe < 1e-3 (=> |delta_lnL| ~ rho^2 * 1e-3 ~ 0.4 nat at rho~20, 3.7x margin to RB_ATOL=1.5) with a much smaller node budget than brute log-spacing. 3) Delete the comment claiming the default 'clears interpolation gate (F within 1e-8 with margin)' (it is false) and replace it with the honest provenance: base count + full-cluster adaptive transition nodes, targeting null-safe max|dF|/max|F| < 1e-3, certified by the RB-vs-brute and interpolation gates. Do NOT touch the spline (not-a-knot, real/imag separate), the delay analytics, the LensedBinningError guard, or any F005/F008 behaviour. If measurement in the gate shows 40 is short for two-image, the documented fallback is to raise the base toward ~82 (proven-safe from the convergence table) — this is surfaced by the acceptance gate, not decided by throwaway Coder probes.
  Who: Coder
  Dependencies: WP1
  Verification: _coarse_w_node_grid places transition nodes at FULL-CLUSTER delay separations (real + virtual-label delays taken from the nearest critical point, mirroring the F008 full-cluster rule) using the now-cheap geometry, with no engine sweep added to grid construction; _DEFAULT_KERNEL_NODES == 40; the false 'F within 1e-8' comment is gone and replaced with honest provenance; production RB-vs-brute |lnlike - lnlike_bruteforce| <= max(1.5, 1e-2*|bf|) holds on every _LENS_CONFIGS row with the shipped default grid, and the null-safe interpolation metric max|dF|/max|F| on the PRODUCTION grid is < 1e-3 for every config; macro-saddle inputs still raise geometry.LensDomainError symmetrically on the RB and brute paths; the spline, delay analytics, LensedBinningError guard and all F005/F008 behaviour are unchanged.
  Max turns: 55

### Professor Inputs
  - ROOT CAUSE of the under-resolution: _coarse_w_node_grid places transition nodes at REAL-image delay separations Delta_j only, but each channel kernel K_a(w) has its smootherstep structure at RHO_END/delta_j where delta_j is the FULL-CLUSTER separation (min over all cluster labels incl. virtual/parked), exactly the real-vs-full-cluster distinction fixed in _channel_switch (F008). Two-image is slow because its structure sits at the virtual-label transitions the grid misses; four-image is fast because all labels are real. FIX = full-cluster transition placement; virtual-label delays come cheaply from geometry.delay at the nearest critical point (so caustic-search acceleration is a prerequisite).
  - F-error -> lnlike-bias mapping: |delta_lnL| ~ rho^2 * (null-safe max|dF|/max|F|). At the fixture's rho~20 (rho^2~400): null-safe 1e-2 -> ~4 nat (FAILS 1.5), 1e-3 -> ~0.4 nat (3.7x margin), 1e-4 -> ~0.04 nat (RB floor). Blessed production interpolation gate = null-safe max|dF|/max|F| < 1e-3; the pointwise-relative 1e-8 metric is ill-posed at interference nulls and must not be used for the gate.
  - Node recommendation: base _DEFAULT_KERNEL_NODES = 20-40 WITH full-cluster transition nodes (effective ~26-30), not a large brute log-spaced default — pure log-spacing needs ~100+ nodes to clear 1e-3 on two-image (n=82 -> 1.1e-3, still marginal). Chosen base=40 as the conservative-but-fast setting; proven-safe fallback toward ~82 if the gate shows 40 short.
  - few-ms is NOT physically reachable this build: F_op's ~2.3 ms/point is a real FLOP floor (order-40 explicit 85x85 njit contraction, ~290k complex ops), not JIT overhead. Caustic elimination (~29 ms) is the one real lever; correct accuracy needs MORE nodes than Build 3, so warm lnlike lands ~50-110 ms single-thread (correct but slower than Build 3's 70 ms). Document the honest floor; the path to few-ms is the deferred, research-grade 2D surrogate table. Do not widen tolerances or fake the ceiling.
  - _contract_orders bit-safety ranking: (i) skipping exact-zero table coefficients is unconditionally F005-safe and bit-identical (untouched cells are IEEE +0.0; 0.0*finite=0.0), gain ~20-30%; (ii) restructuring the matmul / BLAS changes accumulation order (O(eps*condition), condition ~1e6-1e9) and can flip the _CONTRACTION_GUARD=2e-9 / cancellation refusals at the domain boundary — NOT bit-safe without re-certifying vs the 70-dps oracle; (iii) tightening _series_length/MAX_ORDER changes order_used/positive_total/converged and can flip refusals — RISKY. Given the marginal gain, best to attempt none this build.
  - Caustic value-preservation: acceptance is 'returned distance rel < 1e-10 AND identical wave/geometric branch across the suite', not strict bitwise ULP (the distance feeds branch decisions via w*delta_j against a smootherstep of width RHO_END-RHO_START=3.5, so a 1e-10 perturbation is invisible, and the virtual-label delay is quadratically insensitive at the critical point). Multiple near-equal minima on an astroid symmetry axis are benign — related by discrete symmetry, they give the same distance and the same virtual-label delay.

### Domain Test Descriptions
  - PRODUCTION RB-vs-brute gate on EVERY config (re-aim of CrownAccuracyAnchorTestCase). Setup: the existing seeded FastPathTestCase crown fixture (HLV O3 seeded Gaussian noise, IMRPhenomXPHM, par_dic_0), instantiating LensedRelativeBinningLikelihood with the SHIPPED _DEFAULT_KERNEL_NODES (no hard-coded node count in the test — the point is to certify the production default). Operation: for each of the 5 _LENS_CONFIGS rows, evaluate self.like.lnlike(candidate) (production coarse-spline RB path) and self.like.lnlike_bruteforce(candidate) (exact dense amplification, ~10.5 s each, ~1 min total). Expected: both finite and |lnlike - lnlike_bruteforce| <= max(RB_ATOL=1.5, RB_RTOL=1e-2*|bf|) for every config (this is what catches the kappa-config 3.44-nat leak the current crown-only test misses). Also assert both paths raise geometry.LensDomainError symmetrically on a macro-saddle input (1-kappa <= |gamma|). Diagnostic: bar chart of |rb - bf| by config label with the 1.5-nat line drawn.
  - PRODUCTION interpolation gate with a null-safe metric (re-aim of CoarseNodeInterpolationTestCase off the 400-node proxy). Setup: same fixture. For each _LENS_CONFIGS row, build the PRODUCTION coarse node grid by calling self.like._coarse_w_node_grid with the SHIPPED default (never a refined/400-node proxy), evaluate the engine at those nodes, cubic-spline (not-a-knot, real & imag separately) to the dense sub-samples and reconstruct F_interp = sum_a exp(1j w tau_a) K_a. Oracle: F_dense = the engine evaluated DIRECTLY at the same dense sub-sample frequencies and coherently summed by the partition's own reconstructed (F002 — never built from the spline under test). Operation: compute the NULL-SAFE metric epsilon = max_f |F_interp - F_dense| / max_f |F_dense| (well-posed at interference nulls where |F_dense|->0, unlike the pointwise-relative 1e-8 metric which is ill-posed there); also print the pointwise max|dF/F| for information. Expected: epsilon < 1e-3 for every config. Provenance (Professor): |delta_lnL| ~ rho^2 * epsilon; at rho~20, epsilon=1e-3 gives ~0.4 nat, a 3.7x margin to the 1.5-nat RB gate; 1e-3 is subdominant to the RB binning floor's lnlike contribution yet reachable at a modest node budget with full-cluster placement (pure log-spacing needs ~100+ nodes). Diagnostic: per-config overlay of |F_interp - F_dense| (absolute) and |F_interp - F_dense|/max|F_dense| (null-safe) vs w with the 1e-3 line and the RHO_START/RHO_END transition frequencies marked, to expose systematic ringing a scalar gate could average away.
  - SelfFalsification inversion (update of SelfFalsificationTestCase.test_interpolation_gate_rejects_the_default_sparse_grid). The current test PROVES the shipped default fails the interpolation gate; after the node-grid fix the production default must PASS, so the falsification must be re-pointed at a DELIBERATELY under-resolved grid to keep the gate non-vacuous. Setup: same fixture. Operation: build a hard-coded under-resolved grid (n=4 log-spaced nodes, NO transition nodes) for the two-image config, spline-reconstruct F_interp, compare against the direct dense engine F_dense, and compute the same null-safe metric. Expected: epsilon(n=4) > 1e-3 (two-image at n<=12 has null-safe ~0.5, far above 1e-3), proving the interpolation gate CAN go red; and, as a paired positive control, the PRODUCTION default grid PASSES epsilon < 1e-3 on the same config. This shows it is the refinement/placement that buys convergence, not a vacuously loose threshold.
  - Single-thread timing gate (update of FewMsTimingTestCase). Setup: same warm crown fixture, with OMP_NUM_THREADS / MKL_NUM_THREADS / NUMBA_NUM_THREADS pinned to 1 (production is a parallel sampler — every core busy — so the single-thread cost is the real per-eval number). Operation: warm best-of-5 timing of self.like.lnlike vs self.like.lnlike_bruteforce, and of the pure _data_term+_norm_term contraction vs the _amplification_coefficients engine call (inputs drawn from the LIVE hot path). Expected (HARD, machine-independent): lnlike_bruteforce/lnlike >= SPEEDUP_MIN=3.0, and t_contraction < t_amplification_engine. Expected (machine-calibrated regression guard, NOT a physical few-ms claim): warm best-of-5 lnlike <= MS_CEILING (keep 0.25 s as a generous regression guard). Print a per-component breakdown (caustic-search time — expected < 1 ms after WP1 — engine time n_nodes*per_point, contraction time, total lnlike time) so a regression pinpoints the slipped lever and so the change report can quote the honest measured floor. Do NOT tighten MS_CEILING to force few-ms and do NOT recalibrate it to hide the floor.
  - Caustic-search value-preservation (new test for WP1). Setup: a grid of positive-parity lens configurations (several gamma in (0, 0.3], beta in {0, 0.4, 0.7}, kappa in {0, 0.1, 0.3} with 1-kappa>|gamma|, and several source positions spanning inside/near/outside the astroid). Oracle: an INDEPENDENT dense brute-force minimization of the caustic-source distance — evaluate the caustic source point on a very fine theta grid (e.g. 200k angles) in plain numpy (the closed-form critical-curve parametrization, NOT the njit path under test) and take the argmin distance (F002-clean: the oracle shares no code with the accelerated path). Operation: compare geometry.nearest_caustic_point's returned distance against the brute-force oracle. Expected: relative distance error < 1e-10 across the grid; and the wave-vs-geometric branch that channels.select_branch derives from that distance is identical to the branch derived from the oracle distance for a representative set of (config, w) pairs. Diagnostic: scatter of relative distance error vs source-to-caustic distance, flagging any point near an astroid symmetry axis (the benign multiple-minimum case) to confirm the returned distance is still unique there.

